# The modules `make affected` selects among (#1661), one per line, each
# followed by the modules it depends on that no workspace file declares.
# go.work and its go.mod files declare the Go edges, and package.json
# `workspace:` dependencies the pnpm ones; this table holds what neither
# can say: a module reading another's files, building another's
# binary, or running its suites against the stack deploy/local starts.
# Every module go.work or pnpm-workspace.yaml names is listed here, and
# `make affected` fails on one that is not.
#
# `make ci` runs each module's gate in this order, the cheaper Go gates
# before the web ones. A change to a file the root owns selects every
# module; those files are named in ROOT_FILES in tooling/ci/affected.sh.

# check-toolchain reads the platform's go.mod, the console's .nvmrc and
# the stack's Dockerfiles.
tooling platform platform-web deploy/local
lib/errorx
lib/grn
# The platform's Go client generates from the platform's OpenAPI spec.
lib/platform-sdk-go platform
# The platform's suites run against the stack, and drive the client CLI
# they build from garam-cli.
platform garam-cli deploy/local
# The client CLI derives its commands from the platform's and cowork's
# OpenAPI specs, and its coverage test reads them.
garam-cli platform cowork
# cowork's Go client generates from cowork's OpenAPI spec.
lib/cowork-sdk-go cowork
cowork/engine
# cowork's gen builds cowork/engine's bundle into internal/, and its
# suites drive the client CLI they build from garam-cli.
cowork cowork/engine deploy/local garam-cli
# The chart's checks read the environment names the platform, the
# console and the site declare.
deploy/charts platform platform-web site-web
# The stack has no gate of its own; the suites of the modules naming it
# check it.
deploy/local
lib/design
# The platform's client generates its API types from the platform's
# OpenAPI spec, and its tests read the return-path vectors the Go rule
# is tested against.
lib/platform-sdk-ts platform
# The console's browser suite drives the platform's api, and starts the
# site it sends a signed-out visitor to.
platform-web platform deploy/local site-web
# cowork-web generates its API types from cowork's spec, and its browser
# suite drives the cowork binary and signs in through the platform.
cowork-web cowork platform deploy/local
# The site's browser suite drives the platform's api, and signs in to
# the console it hands a visitor to.
site-web platform deploy/local platform-web
